<p>Yes. You can pay someone to apply for jobs for you, and the cost depends on who does the work: ApplyScout (Scout) charges $39 to $999 a month, with AI Assistant plans at $39 or $79 and Human Assistant plans at $299, $499 or $999, and Career Agents publishes roughly $1,500 to $4,500 a month for reverse recruiters (post dated August 3, 2026, fetched November 5, 2026). My Personal Recruiter states $50 to $300 a month for application services and $2,000 to $5,000 a month for reverse recruiters (page updated October 27, 2026, fetched November 5, 2026). You are paying for application work: finding suitable openings, preparing your materials, completing the forms and recording what was sent. Employers still decide who gets interviewed and hired, so no honest provider can promise either.</p>
